      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In 18 patients with clinically confirmed arteriosclerosis, angina pectoris attacks and myocardial infarction, a distinct recession of catecholamines (adrenalin and noradrenalin were determined separately) was found in urine, also, a normalization of blood fat parameters. Frequency and intensity of angina pectoris attacks regressed. It is discussed that these effects might be explained by the special composition of VisanoCor."},
